1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,450
Vikings. Raiders. Horned helmets.

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:04,950
Except... no.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,450
Vikings never wore horned helmets.

4
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:09,950
In 1943, a Norwegian farmer dug up a Viking helmet.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,450
The only near-complete one ever found.

6
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:14,950
Horns: zero.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,450
Horns in a fight? Great way to get grabbed.

8
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:19,950
So where did the horns come from?

9
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,450
Horned helmets did exist. In Bronze Age Denmark.

10
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:24,950
About 1,700 years before the Vikings.

11
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,450
Probably ceremonial. Historians still argue.

12
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:29,950
Then 1800s artists painted Vikings with horns.

13
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,450
Because it looked cool.

14
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:34,950
In 1876, Wagner's opera costumes went all in.

15
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,450
Audiences loved it.

16
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:39,950
The horns stuck.

17
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,450
Now they're on every costume and cartoon.

18
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:44,950
Real Vikings? Round helmets. No horns.

19
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,450
Horns: still zero.

20
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:49,950
Anyway, here's the wrong version again.
